# Ansible Project Conventions

## Playbook Style

- Use fully qualified collection names (e.g., `ansible.builtin.debug`, not `debug`)
- Use `ansible.builtin.shell` when pipes (`|`) are needed, `ansible.builtin.command` otherwise
- Mark sensitive tasks with `no_log: true` only in production; remove during troubleshooting
- Always set `changed_when` and `failed_when` for command/shell tasks

## Target Environment

- RHEL9 execution nodes with SELinux enforcing
- AAP containerized installer (not OpenShift)
- Execution Environments run as podman containers
- Teleport v17 configuration syntax (`version: v2`, `outputs` not `destinations`)

## Variables

- Teleport-specific variables are prefixed with `teleport_`
- System/directory variables are prefixed with `tbot_`
- Sensitive variables (`teleport_admin_password`, `teleport_mfa_token`) must use `no_log: true`
